{"node":{"id":"HP:0009710","label":"Chilblains","ic":6.897,"definition":"Chilblains, also called perniosis, are an inflammatory skin condition related to an abnormal vascular response to the cold. We are unaware of a reliable estimate of incidence. It typically presents as tender, pruritic red or bluish lesions located symmetrically on the dorsal aspect of the fingers, toes, ears and nose. Less commonly, reports describe involvement of the thighs and buttocks. The lesions present hours after exposure to cold and usually resolve spontaneously in one to three weeks."},"diseases":[{"id":"MONDO:0018866","label":"Aicardi-Goutieres syndrome","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_b7a4969661f9","source":"MONDO:0018866","target":"HP:0009710","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:51 · ORPHA:51","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/51","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.6,"snippet":"Aicardi-Goutières syndrome: Chilblains (frequency HP:0040282) [TAS]"},{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:51","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/51","confidence":0.6,"snippet":"Chilblains — Frequent (79-30%)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.6,"independent_sources":["Orphanet"],"level":"curated"},"confidence":0.6},{"id":"MONDO:0013059","label":"Aicardi-Goutieres syndrome 5","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_f7d24aa26494","source":"MONDO:0013059","target":"HP:0009710","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"OMIM","record":"OMIM:612952 · PMID:19525956","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19525956/","level":"observed","date":"2023-03-26","confidence":0.57,"snippet":"Aicardi-Goutieres syndrome 5: Chilblains (frequency 8/14) [PCS]"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.57,"independent_sources":["OMIM"],"level":"observed"},"confidence":0.57},{"id":"MONDO:0012471","label":"Aicardi-Goutieres syndrome 3","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_b342444d6a5e","source":"